/*
 * Code blocks in these articles contain long single-line prompts (a 700px-wide
 * ```markdown block in the Claude Fable 5 piece), and the theme's
 * .line-numbers-mode wrapper measured ~8px wider than a 390px viewport on
 * mobile, which pushed the whole document into horizontal scroll.
 *
 * Constrain the wrapper and let the <pre> scroll inside it, rather than hiding
 * overflow at the document level: the prompt text still has to be reachable,
 * and a page that scrolls sideways on a phone is worse than one that scrolls
 * a code block.
 */
div[class*="language-"]
  max-width 100%
  pre
    max-width 100%
    overflow-x auto
